Z||000000||Vlad||06-28-2001||10:25 PM||||I'm thinking of installing set of smaller pulleys from Summit Racing for my 85 GT Auto.<P>Now I heard that since alternator will spin slower, installing this set would reduce voltage in the system.<P>How true is it? Any consequenses? Anybody has a problem with this set?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||06-28-2001||11:28 PM||||I have a power pulley on my auto. The only<BR>time charging becomes an issue is if you are stopped with your headlights on and the fan turns on. The guage will start to read below 13. This only happens when you're sitting on<BR>your brakes for a long time with the fan and lights all on at once.<BR>If this happens just throw it into neutral and watch the guage, you might have to push the gas pedal down a little to bring the charge back up. When the light turns green take your foot off the gas, put it back in gear, and go.<P>I've had it on for a couple-a years now and that's the only prob. i've had with it and believe me it's well worth it!<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000002||DecadenceR||06-28-2001||11:49 PM||||Do they make those pulleys for the Duke?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||06-28-2001||11:55 PM||||I've never heard of any pulley's for the Duke but that doesn't mean there aren't any.<BR>Fiero Conversions still sells a turbo for the Duke though.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
